                <pb facs="0343" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00 Elections/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-21T11:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. This morning the Council of State sitting as National Assembly unanimously
                    elected Eugene Roy President of Haiti. Twenty-one votes cast. I shall
                    immediately recognize Mr. Roy as the Presidentelect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
